Z||000000||nova||07-09-99||11:13 PM||||<br>i just bought a 1987, 4cld, fiero and the oil pressure gauge is going from 40 to pegging out of sight, i don't no if it's a messed up gauge or something wrong serious. anyone ever heard of it before please email or post message for me, thanks
Z||000001||Lynx||07-10-99||02:54 AM||||My car has the same problem right NOW. I have had this happen in other cars so i know how to fix it just havent yet. The gauge is fine but the sensor on the block is bad. Pegging out is usually what happens when they go bad. It on the block beside the distributer. you just unhook it and it unscrews out. The cheapest sensor i have found is $32.99 (thats why i havent cared to fix it yet). Remeber to get the one with 3 connections and no the single connection sensor.<p>Lynx
